---
/**
 * Terms of Use for mannpatel.me. Plain-language website terms for a sole proprietor in
 * Ontario. They describe how the site really works (enquiries are not contracts; work is
 * agreed in a written scope). Not legal advice: have a lawyer review before relying on them.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/site';

const updated = '1 November 2026';
const email = profile.contact.email;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of Use for mannpatel.me: using the website, enquiries and quotes, project examples, content ownership, links, liability and Ontario law."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="label">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="lead">The rules for using mannpatel.me, in plain language.</p>
      <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}. See also the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>About these terms</h2>
      <p>
        This website is run by {profile.name}, a sole proprietor in Toronto, Ontario, Canada. By using it, you agree to
        these terms. If you don’t agree, please don’t use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Information on this site</h2>
      <p>
        The pages describe my services and past work in general terms. They aren’t professional, legal or financial
        advice for your situation. I keep them accurate and up to date as best I can, but services, availability and
        details can change without notice.
      </p>

      <h2>Enquiries and quotes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Sending a brief, an email, a call or a message is a request for a conversation. It isn’t a contract or a booking.</li>
        <li>
          Any work is agreed in a written scope and quote that lists the deliverables, exclusions, price and timing. If
          that agreement says something different from this page, the agreement applies.
        </li>
        <li>I can decline a project, for example if it isn’t something I do well.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Project examples</h2>
      <p>
        The Work pages show real projects, each labelled with its status (live or in progress). Anything fictional, such
        as the sample enquiry on the home page, is marked “Sample”. Client names, logos and screenshots belong to their
        owners and are shown with permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Content ownership</h2>
      <p>
        Unless stated otherwise, the text, design, logo and photos on this site belong to {profile.name}. You may share
        links to any page. Please don’t copy the content or design for commercial use without written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Please don’t misuse the site: no spam or automated submissions through the form, no attempts to break, overload
        or gain unauthorised access to it, and no harmful code.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>
        Links to other sites (such as Nest &amp; Rest Cleaning, client websites or social profiles) are for convenience.
        I’m not responsible for their content or their privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided “as is”. To the extent the law allows, I’m not liable for any loss that comes from using it
        or relying on its general information. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under Ontario consumer
        protection law that can’t be waived.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>How information you send is handled is explained in the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada that apply there.</p>

      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        If these terms change, this page is updated and the date at the top changes with it.
        {email && <> Questions: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</>}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: calc(var(--container-text) + 2 * var(--gutter));
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-s);
  }
  h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.3em;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
  }
</style>
